用了普通的面料并进行了纹饰处理的布衣，衣服的边缘处也添加了简单的纹饰。","en":"A cloth garment made of ordinary fabric with decorative patterning, finished with simple trim along its edges."},"defenceVal":"2","mp":"340","price":"1200","slot":{"zh":"护甲","en":"Armor"}},{"id":"WP1026905","name":{"zh":"巧士冠","en":"Artisan Crown"},"level":"2","description":{"zh":"更为精致的小冠，多为朝中职务多面之人佩戴。","en":"A more refined small crown, mostly worn by court officials serving in multiple capacities."},"mp":"670","evade":"10","price":"6000","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{},"clans":[{"id":"GI112315","name":{"zh":"襄阳向氏","en":"The Xiang clan of Xiangyang"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"出自子姓，春秋宋桓公之后，食邑于向（今河南济源），后裔以向为氏。汉代迁居荆州襄阳郡宜城县，至汉末已成为当地望族。向朗师从司马徽，与庞统、徐庶为友，历任巴西、牂牁、房陵太守，领丞相长史；向宠为诸葛亮在《出师表》中称赞的将领，掌管宿卫兵；向充在诸葛亮去世后上表请立庙于沔阳。","en":"Originating from the Zi surname as descendants of Duke Huan of Song in the Spring and Autumn period, they received Xiang (present-day Jiyuan, Henan) as their fief, and their descendants adopted Xiang as their surname. During the Han dynasty, they relocated to Yicheng County, Xiangyang Commandery, Jing Province, becoming a prominent local family by the late Han. Xiang Lang studied under Sima Hui and befriended Pang Tong and Xu Shu, he successively served as Governor of Baxi, Zangke, and Fangling, and held the post of Chief Clerk to the Chancellor. Xiang Chong was a general praised by Zhuge Liang in his 'Memorial on the Expedition', commanding the imperial bodyguards. After Zhuge Liang's passing, Xiang Chong petitioned to erect a temple in his honor at Mianyang."},"talent":{"military":"5","commerce":"2","politics":"4"}}],"friendGroups":[{"story":"S10302","members":["WJ10085","WJ10203","WJ10116","WJ10370","WJ10017"]},{"story":"S10602","members":["WJ10011","WJ10370","WJ10379","WJ10385","WJ10513"]}],"body":null,"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","nam